Article 29

(1) Forms of community participation may include:

a. Supervision; or
b. Provision of assistance;
(2) Community supervision includes activities:
a. observing or seeing the condition of the fulfillment of the rights of women and children; and b. providing information on any conditions that tend to lead to acts of violence against women and children to police officers and/or local government.
(3) The provision of assistance as referred to in paragraph (1) letter b is in the form of: a. security or temporary shelter for victims;

. b. financial support to meet the needs of victims according to the capacity of the community;

c. Financial and/or facility assistance to the local government in supporting the implementation of protection for women and children.
